---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import AppCta from '../components/AppCta.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About Stocker and our editorial approach"
  description="Meet the purpose behind Stocker and learn how we write guides, compare products, source company information, and handle corrections."
  ><div class="container text-page">
    <h1>About Stocker</h1><div class="prose">
      <p>
        Stocker helps people discover companies and organize a stock research
        list. This website is published by the team behind the Stocker app,
        listed on the App Store under Yoav Tzori.
      </p><p>
        We write for people who want to understand the business behind a ticker.
        The aim is a clearer question, a useful explanation, or a practical next
        step in research.
      </p><h2 id="editorial-policy">How we write</h2><ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Sources come first.</strong> We link to company disclosures, product
          documentation and educational sources so you can check the original information.
        </li><li>
          <strong>Examples are labelled.</strong> Fictional figures explain a calculation.
          They are not live market data or forecasts.
        </li><li>
          <strong>Our relationship is visible.</strong> We make Stocker. App comparisons
          disclose that relationship and explain when another product may fit a different
          task.
        </li><li>
          <strong>Methods matter.</strong> A documentation-based comparison is described
          that way. We do not claim hands-on testing or independent scoring without
          evidence.
        </li><li>
          <strong>Uncertainty stays visible.</strong> Company comparisons describe
          business differences and research questions. They do not promise returns
          or select an investment for you.
        </li>
      </ul><h2>Authors and review</h2><p>
        Articles are attributed to the Stocker team. We do not present the site
        as a licensed investment advisory service or claim a qualified financial
        reviewer has checked an article unless one is explicitly named. Source
        links and publication dates make the basis of each piece visible.
      </p><h2>Updates and corrections</h2><p>
        Product features and company information change. Check the dated source
        material, particularly before relying on a price, forecast or feature.
        To report a problem, use the support contact provided through our <a
          href={SITE.appStore}>App Store listing</a
        >.
      </p><h2>What this site does not do</h2><p>
        We do not execute trades, provide individualized investment advice, or
        guarantee that an app, metric or research process will produce a return.
        Calculators use the values you supply and explain the assumptions they
        leave out.
      </p>
    </div><AppCta />
  </div></SiteLayout
>
